{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpanningForest","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdditiveArithmetic","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ties."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Edges are ordered by weight, then by position in "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Under that strict order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the minimum spanning forest is unique, and this is it, whichever algorithm runs: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"canonical forest, listed in nondecreasing weight and, among equal weights, in position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, with the weight added up in that order. Currently Kruskal’s algorithm on sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graphs (fewer than 4 edges per vertex) and otherwise Prim’s under that order followed by a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sort of the n − 1 edges taken, which is faster on denser graphs (see the benchmarks)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each edge’s weight from its position, so parallel edges can differ. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once for each edge that is not a self-loop, never for a self-loop, and not kept."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Negative and zero weights are ordinary weights, and so are infinities. A NaN weight traps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(NetworkX instead offers "},{"code":"ignore_nan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; filter such edges out first)."}]},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m log m)."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No weight is NaN; the sum of the chosen weights, in the order listed, does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not overflow and is not NaN.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P13SpanningTreesE07minimumC4Tree6weightAD0C6ForestVyxqd__Gqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"SpanningTrees","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Kruskal.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpanningTrees\/Kruskal.swift#L24"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumSpanningTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SpanningForest","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"title":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A minimum spanning forest: one minimum spanning tree per connected component (NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and igraph’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimum_spanning_tree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","title":"SpanningTrees","role":"collection","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols":{"type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[]},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/SpanningForest":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpanningForest","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SpanningForest","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A spanning forest of an undirected graph: one spanning tree per connected component, as edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions in the graph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":", with the sum of their weights (JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SpanningTree"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getWeight"},{"type":"text","text":" these are)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/spanningforest","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SpanningForest","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumSpanni